{"name":"Tanzanite","hex":"#1478a7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tanzanite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trichroic violet-blue variety of the mineral zoisite mined in Tanzania, used as a gemstone. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tanzanite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tanzanite","blocks":[{"text":"Tanzanite is the blue and violet variety of the mineral zoisite. The color is caused by small amounts of vanadium. Tanzanite belongs to the epidote mineral group. Tanzanite is only found in Simanjiro District of Manyara Region in Tanzania, in a very small mining area approximately 7 km (4.3 mi) long and 2 km (1.2 mi) wide near the Mererani Hills."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Zo%C3%AFsite_%28Tanzanite%29.jpg/330px-Zo%C3%AFsite_%28Tanzanite%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanzanite"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg/500px-Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg/500px-Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Craft work on tanzanite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACraft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam